# Phase 4 — Firewall & Security Rules

# Inspect the current iptables firewall configuration
sudo iptables -L -n -v

# -L: List the firewall rules
# -n: Display IP addresses and ports numerically
# -v: Display detailed information and packet/byte counters

# The command displays the main firewall chains:
# INPUT   -> Traffic entering the system
# FORWARD -> Traffic passing through the system
# OUTPUT  -> Traffic leaving the system

# The command also shows the default policy of each chain
# and the number of packets and bytes processed by the rules.

# Practical result:
# INPUT policy: ACCEPT
# FORWARD policy: ACCEPT
# OUTPUT policy: ACCEPT
# No visible filtering rules were configured.
# Packet and byte counters were 0.